From 08f561b530b1fa4c125d4bf6824309909bdede7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:43:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/21] sgx/compiler: add the fixed programs and the unit tests

sgx_fixed.c holds the fixed USSE programs a frame needs besides the
shaders: the TA state-emit programs, the empty task, the clear's and the
viewport object's vertex programs, the copy and uniform-colour pixel
programs, the position-only vertex programs and the pixel-event tasks. They
are assembly text, assembled through the isa library when a context is
created; a golden header checks the words they assemble to.

The gtest suite (meson test --suite sgx) builds shaders with nir_builder,
compiles them and checks that every word decodes through the isaspec
disassembler: 55 cases covering varyings, co-issue, loops, textures, the
colour fast paths, mediump and lowp arithmetic, discard, constants past the
register file, and the fixed programs. README.md describes the compiler's structure and its
debug flags (SGX_COMPILER_DEBUG).

